{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And when a soul brings a meal-offering.</b> Whose way is it to donate a meal-offering — the poor person's. Said HaKadosh Baruch Hu: I account it for him as though he offered his very soul (Menachot 104:). And for this reason it is stated in parashat Tzav (Leviticus 6:9) ״מַצּוֹת תֵּאָכֵל״, which is to say לֶחֶם עֹנִי, poor man's bread, and the poor — for all of this belongs to the poor person who is humble by nature, like the nature of matzah which does not rise. And along these lines the order of all these offerings shall be explained: and whatever comes first in the verse comes first in coming to sin, as it says (Deuteronomy 32:15) ״וַיִּשְׁמַן יְשֻׁרוּן וַיִּבְעָט״. And whoever is greater than his fellow in wealth or in honor, his evil inclination is greater than his, and the proof is from what is said (Leviticus 4:22) ״אֲשֶׁר נָשִׂיא יֶחֱטָא״ — for the word ״אֲשֶׁר״ indicates certainty, because his office of leadership brings him to sin, since his inclination is greater than his fellow's. Therefore He mentioned first the cattle, for presumably the one who offers it is wealthy, and afterward He mentioned sheep, for it is the way of the intermediate person to bring sheep, and afterward He mentioned the bird-offering, for it is the way of the poor person to bring a bird, and afterward He mentioned the meal-offering, which is brought by one who is at the extreme of poverty." "And therefore it is stated regarding the cattle: ״וְקִרְבּוֹ וּכְרָעָיו יִרְחַץ בַּמַּיִם״ — that is, the innards of the offering; but the innards of the man and the deep heart were not washed, and their impurity is still upon them, for in most cases wealth causes the kicking and its filth is not washed. But the intermediate person — his thoughts are purer; therefore it is stated of him ״וְהַקֶּרֶב וְהַכְּרָעַיִם יִרְחַץ בַּמַּיִם״, to include also the innards of the man who brings the offering — that by means of the offering he returns and is comforted regarding the evil, and his innards are washed through with waters of purity. But the poor person, for whom HaShem is his refuge — his thoughts are purer than them all; it is stated of him ״וְהֵסִיר אֶת מֻרְאָתָהּ בְּנֹצָתָהּ וְהִשְׁלִיךְ אֹתָהּ״ — this removal and casting away is better than washing, a hint that he casts from his innards all iniquity, and an upright heart is renewed within him, and he brings out the old on account of the new. And one who is at the extreme of poverty, who is humbled more than all and whose eyes are always lifted toward HaShem — it is stated of him ״וְנֶפֶשׁ כִּי תַקְרִיב״, for not only does he cast from within himself all inner deceit, but his entire soul he offers as a whole-offering to HaShem, and all of him is made a new creation. Therefore it is stated of this meal-offering: ״קֹדֶשׁ קָדָשִׁים מֵאִשֵּׁי ה׳״ — that is to say, more than the offerings by fire to HaShem that were mentioned above."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:35:10.251765694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}